      {
        "question": "where is it found?",
        "prediction": "The oribi is found in eastern, southern, and western Africa. Specific protected areas where it occurs include:\n\n*   **Nigeria**: Gashaka Gumti National Park\n*   **Benin**: Pendjari and W National Parks\n*   **Chad**: Aouk Hunting Zone\n*   **Cameroon**: Benoue, Bouba Njida and Faro National Parks\n*   **Central African Republic**: Manovo-Gounda St. Floris National Park\n*   **Congo-Kinshasa**: Garamba, Upemba and Kundelungu National Parks\n*   **Ethiopia**: Omo National Park\n*   **Kenya**: Masai Mara Game Reserve and Ruma National Park\n*   **South Africa**: Golden Gate Highlands National Park\n*   **Tanzania**: Serengeti National Park\n*   **Uganda**: Kidepo Valley, Lake Mburo and Murchison Falls National Parks\n*   **Zambia**: Kafue and Liuwa Plain National Parks and Bangweulu Swamp",
